# .inspiration

Reference sites and ideas that should shape work on seanmh.com.

**How to use this file.** Read it before design work — a new version branch, a
redesign, a hero, a loader, a work/project index, typography or palette
decisions. It is not a spec and nothing here should be copied literally. It is a
record of *why* particular sites work, so that a choice made here can be argued
from something real instead of from defaults. When a decision on this site
echoes something below, say which entry and which principle.

**Adding to it.** New entries go under "Sites" with the same shape: what it is,
what is concretely on it, what technique is worth stealing, what to avoid.
Record measured facts (hex values, type stacks, section names, URLs) rather than
adjectives — a future model cannot re-derive "it feels premium," but it can act
on `--color--lime: #d2ff00`.

Last surveyed: 2026-09-19 (kengoworks AI-authored sites walked in depth the same day).

---

## Sites

### 1. kengoworks.com — Kengo Works, by Kevin Ngo

*The newest and most relevant reference. A one-person creative studio publishing
work made with frontier models, presented as a museum rather than a portfolio.*

- Site: https://www.kengoworks.com/  (bare `kengoworks.com` redirects to `www`)
- Author: Kevin Ngo — X: https://x.com/kevin_t_ngo
- Support: https://stripe.com/@kevinngo · Games: https://kengoworks.itch.io/
- Tagline: "Generative art, short films, and experimental games."
- Masthead: "Kengo Works — Kevin Ngo". Nav is three items only: About,
  Support, Follow me on X. Footer is one line: "© 2026 kengoworks".
- Stack: Next.js on Vercel. Sits behind a Vercel bot checkpoint (see
  "Fetching notes" at the bottom of this file).

#### The complete body of work (13 pieces, all dated 2026)

Grouped on the homepage by medium. The `NN/13` index is the prev/next tour
order, which deliberately differs from the sidebar grouping.

